{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbJYswiHZg5XfAWbjwYv", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`git rebase --onto` transplants a range of commits onto a new base. The full form is:\n\n```\ngit rebase --onto <newbase> <upstream> [<branch>]\n```\n\nIt takes the commits reachable from `<branch>` (default: `HEAD`) but not from `<upstream>`, and replays them on top of `<newbase>`. Plain `git rebase main` is the shortcut where `<newbase>` and `<upstream>` are the same.\n\n**Example:** you branched `feature` off `topic`, but `topic` shouldn't be part of your history. You want `feature` to sit directly on `main`.\n\n```\nBefore:\nmain:     A---B\n               \\\ntopic:          C---D\n                     \\\nfeature:              E---F\n\ngit rebase --onto main topic feature\n\nAfter:\nmain:     A---B\n              |\\\n              | E'---F'    (feature)\n              \\\ntopic:          C---D\n```\n\n- `topic..feature` selects `E` and `F`, the commits on `feature` that aren't on `topic`.\n- They are replayed onto `main` as new commits `E'` and `F'`.\n- `feature` now points at `F'`. `topic` is untouched.\n\n**Common uses:**\n- Move a branch off another branch, as above.\n- Drop a range of commits from the middle: `git rebase --onto A B` removes the commits after `B`, up to `HEAD`, from the history after `A`.\n- Move a branch after its parent was squash-merged: `git rebase --onto main <old-parent-tip> feature`.\n\nThe rebased commits get new hashes. If the branch was already pushed, you'll need `git push --force-with-lease`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6686, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11903, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6686}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3e1fc8f3-621b-4f48-a7c0-452e57210b08", "uuid": "a51dadd5-18a5-4cc2-b3bf-164229c7a79c", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:45:49.965Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbJYsiLAN5FsEKEwwCnB"}
